WEBVTT

00:03.253 --> 00:05.964
<i>Causes of death are many and varied.</i>

00:06.047 --> 00:09.634
<i>Old age, suicide, illness…</i>

00:09.718 --> 00:14.180
<i>But the cause of death that scares</i>
<i>the most people in this day and age…</i>

00:17.934 --> 00:19.102
<i>…is death by fire.</i>

00:42.041 --> 00:45.211
Sister Sumire…

02:24.435 --> 02:27.105
Sister Sumire…

02:27.188 --> 02:29.190
Why are you here?

02:29.274 --> 02:32.569
I should ask the same of you.
What business do you have here?

02:35.738 --> 02:37.240
Oh, my…

02:43.496 --> 02:47.625
You were reading without
permission again, Sister Hibana.

02:50.628 --> 02:54.507
I taught you countless times
to clean up after yourself.

02:54.591 --> 02:57.468
You knew of this place.

02:59.345 --> 03:02.932
The fire… The cause of everything…

03:04.601 --> 03:07.478
Did you come here
seeking the answer to that?

03:08.688 --> 03:12.358
Sister Sumire, what were
you doing down here?

03:12.442 --> 03:16.237
Oh? I thought you had
already found your answer.

03:20.199 --> 03:21.784
Doppelgangers?

03:21.868 --> 03:23.244
Yes, yes.

03:23.328 --> 03:25.455
You were always so
diligent in your studies.

03:25.538 --> 03:28.708
You always asked the adults
if you were right.

03:28.791 --> 03:30.293
Oh, the memories.

03:31.252 --> 03:34.714
Enough bullshit! Tell me
what you were doing down here!

03:34.797 --> 03:37.467
Oh? Jumping straight to the answer?

03:37.550 --> 03:39.010
That isn't like you--

03:40.011 --> 03:45.099
You used the sisters here
in experiments on doppelgangers!

03:45.183 --> 03:49.520
You fooled devout children
to create pyrokinetics!

03:51.314 --> 03:54.192
The sisters were all so innocent.

03:54.275 --> 03:59.197
Precisely! We all loved you!

03:59.280 --> 04:01.032
You used our faith…

04:02.825 --> 04:07.288
…to add Adolla insects
to the vegetables you fed us!

04:07.372 --> 04:10.500
Feed people bugs to create pyrokinetics?!

04:10.583 --> 04:11.417
How does that work?!

04:11.501 --> 04:13.628
This is the secret
behind human combustion!

04:14.796 --> 04:18.341
<i>The mass combustion of the sisters here</i>

04:18.925 --> 04:22.762
<i>was one of Sister Sumire's</i>
<i>experiments on doppelgangers!</i>

04:23.638 --> 04:26.599
<i>A doppelganger is another self</i>
<i>contained within Adolla.</i>

04:27.267 --> 04:29.686
She was trying to
summon them into this world.

04:29.769 --> 04:32.480
And the tool to summon them…

04:32.563 --> 04:34.023
are those insects?!

04:35.233 --> 04:37.568
Insects are creatures from Adolla.

04:37.652 --> 04:40.405
They must be a bridge
between it and this world.

04:41.406 --> 04:47.370
<i>In Adolla, there are as many other selves</i>
<i>as there are people in this world.</i>

04:47.996 --> 04:51.082
When they interact and assimilate
with their selves in this world,

04:51.165 --> 04:53.793
that is when human combustion occurs!

04:55.003 --> 04:57.380
<i>What on earth is this Adolla?!</i>

05:16.482 --> 05:22.363
Very well done, Sister Hibana.
You have found that much of the answer.

05:22.447 --> 05:28.077
An intelligent child remains
intelligent after they grow up.

05:31.789 --> 05:33.207
An earthquake?

05:33.291 --> 05:35.626
What are these pillars for?

05:35.710 --> 05:39.005
Thanks to the experiments,
all of the Pillars have assembled.

05:39.088 --> 05:41.132
The Pillars have assembled?

05:41.215 --> 05:44.302
You were performing experiments
to create Adolla Bursts as well?

05:45.678 --> 05:50.767
How many lives of the orphans here
did you toy with in your experiments?!

05:52.894 --> 05:55.480
Perhaps we should end
the conversation now.

05:56.522 --> 06:00.151
You will be buried alive here.

06:00.860 --> 06:03.362
When did you start
performing the experiments?!

06:04.155 --> 06:09.952
Was this convent your laboratory
long before we were ever raised?

06:12.455 --> 06:13.873
Another earthquake?!

06:18.169 --> 06:19.045
Hibana! Fire!

06:22.340 --> 06:23.257
Just from touching it?!

06:24.967 --> 06:26.594
It is cold down here.

06:29.847 --> 06:32.016
You must be Karim.

06:32.100 --> 06:34.310
Stealing my heat in an instant?

06:35.019 --> 06:38.022
Rekka was so passionate.
He was such a handful.

06:38.106 --> 06:44.028
<i>And he had such a desire for justice. He</i>
<i>prayed fervently for salvation of flame.</i>

06:45.488 --> 06:47.615
You raised Rekka too?!

06:47.698 --> 06:50.701
What on earth are you trying to do?!

06:50.785 --> 06:54.122
You have always been so curious.

06:54.205 --> 06:56.916
I will tell you
as a reward before you die.

06:57.583 --> 07:00.711
<i>250 years ago, before</i>
<i>human combustion occurred,</i>

07:01.671 --> 07:04.757
<i>the Great Cataclysm was a failure.</i>

07:04.841 --> 07:07.635
<i>Without enough Pillars or energy,</i>

07:07.718 --> 07:11.264
<i>the world was rent apart,</i>
<i>and embers remained.</i>

07:13.683 --> 07:17.854
Ever since
the last Great Cataclysm failed,

07:17.937 --> 07:21.941
I have been creating new Pillars
for the next Great Cataclysm.

07:22.024 --> 07:25.445
From 250 years ago?

07:25.528 --> 07:27.655
What on earth are you?

07:27.738 --> 07:30.992
There was no human combustion
before the Great Cataclysm?

07:31.492 --> 07:33.786
Then what was the Great Cataclysm?!

07:33.870 --> 07:35.872
That is enough for your reward.

07:35.955 --> 07:39.333
But it truly is cold today.

07:41.210 --> 07:42.920
Another earthquake?

07:43.004 --> 07:45.631
The attack before
used very powerful vibrations.

07:46.299 --> 07:48.050
Are these earthquakes also…

07:48.759 --> 07:50.386
What on earth is your power?!

07:51.929 --> 07:56.809
The reason I came here was,
more than the mysteries of the world…

07:59.353 --> 08:04.317
…to get revenge on the ones who took
the lives of my precious friends!

08:05.860 --> 08:09.489
Do you really think that they all died?

08:18.247 --> 08:19.832
Hibana…

08:19.916 --> 08:21.792
It's hot…

08:21.876 --> 08:24.754
Demons?! Child demons?!

08:24.837 --> 08:28.716
H-H-Hibana…

08:30.218 --> 08:31.886
Sakura?

08:31.969 --> 08:34.096
It hurts…

08:34.180 --> 08:35.598
Hiba…

08:35.681 --> 08:37.850
Hibana…

08:43.731 --> 08:47.485
You… What did you…

08:47.568 --> 08:49.362
You know who these are?

08:49.445 --> 08:53.324
As Head Sister, I let you see
each other one last time.

08:53.407 --> 08:56.786
Hell is very close to you.

09:02.041 --> 09:02.917
Huo Yan, get back!

09:05.795 --> 09:08.297
You will hurt yourself if you touch me.

09:08.381 --> 09:10.967
Karim, her power…

09:11.050 --> 09:14.011
It seems she's vibrating her body
to turn it into a weapon.

09:14.679 --> 09:17.515
Offense and defense using vibrations.

09:17.598 --> 09:22.728
But how can she use pyrokinesis
to generate that much vibration?

09:23.312 --> 09:27.817
It is a natural reaction
for biological organisms: shivering.

09:28.526 --> 09:31.070
I shiver because it is cold.

09:31.153 --> 09:34.657
I simply amplify my shivering.

09:34.740 --> 09:40.413
Shivering is a biological reaction
to the cold where the body shakes.

09:40.496 --> 09:44.125
Is she using that to generate
those ultrasonic vibrations?

09:44.208 --> 09:48.004
But if the earthquakes that keep happening

09:48.087 --> 09:51.465
are part of her power…

09:51.549 --> 09:53.926
What the hell are you?!

09:54.010 --> 09:59.640
Even with a pyrokinetic ability,
shaking the earth itself is impossible…

09:59.724 --> 10:02.977
…unless she uses an Adolla Burst!

10:10.276 --> 10:12.528
Captain Hibana! Are you safe?!

10:12.612 --> 10:14.488
Well done, Kishiri! Help us!

10:14.572 --> 10:16.449
Heh. She praised me.

10:17.992 --> 10:21.162
You children do like making trouble.

10:23.331 --> 10:25.166
She stopped moving!

10:25.249 --> 10:27.209
We need to get out right now!

10:33.215 --> 10:35.885
Sister Sumire…

10:36.677 --> 10:39.055
You are up to this once again?

10:39.639 --> 10:41.182
Oh, what a surprise.

10:41.807 --> 10:45.019
I will only rot away now.

10:46.270 --> 10:51.651
I used the last of my
power to make contact.

10:51.734 --> 10:55.655
You were always a worrywart,
even 250 years ago.

10:55.738 --> 11:00.576
It is futile now. The human world
is bound for destruction.

11:02.995 --> 11:05.206
You have never changed…

11:06.165 --> 11:11.128
From 250 years ago when, just like me,

11:11.712 --> 11:14.590
you became a Pillar…

11:26.519 --> 11:28.437
Struggle all you wish.

11:33.025 --> 11:35.444
Farewell, Woman in Black.

11:35.945 --> 11:39.865
I will fulfill my duty
as the Seventh Pillar.

11:47.415 --> 11:50.418
But I must say, it is so cold.

11:50.501 --> 11:52.628
There is not enough flame.

11:58.384 --> 12:00.261
The earthquakes stopped.

12:00.344 --> 12:02.388
It doesn't seem like
she's chasing after us.

12:07.017 --> 12:08.269
Sakura…

12:08.978 --> 12:10.521
Clematis…

12:10.604 --> 12:12.106
Huh? What is it? You talking about me?

12:12.189 --> 12:14.275
Shut up. Silence, gravel.

12:14.358 --> 12:16.110
What do we do now?

12:16.777 --> 12:22.283
The cause of human combustion was
doppelgangers from the other world Adolla

12:22.366 --> 12:27.079
interacting with people in this world…

12:27.872 --> 12:31.041
Then the Great Cataclysm
is a combustion reaction

12:31.125 --> 12:37.465
which occurs when Adolla itself interacts
with the entirety of this world.

12:38.340 --> 12:40.426
To turn the Earth into the Sun…

12:40.509 --> 12:41.635
What?!

12:42.303 --> 12:46.140
That's what one of the White-Clad
named Haumea said at the Imperial Seat.

12:47.433 --> 12:50.853
If the Pillars all gather
at the Evangelist,

12:50.936 --> 12:53.063
the Great Cataclysm will occur again,

12:53.147 --> 12:56.400
enveloping the world in flames
and destroying it…

12:57.193 --> 13:00.446
<i>We need to do something</i>
<i>to prevent another Great Cataclysm!</i>

13:08.996 --> 13:10.873
ASAKUSA

13:31.435 --> 13:32.895
I am a knight…

13:48.327 --> 13:50.454
I held my holy sword…

13:57.294 --> 13:59.547
Was it the holy sword?

14:11.100 --> 14:13.727
The remains of Excalibur?

14:13.811 --> 14:17.356
Heat-resistant carbon. You can find this
at any home improvement store.

14:17.940 --> 14:19.149
It is orichalcum.

14:19.233 --> 14:22.736
O-Orichalcum?
You mean the fictitious metal?

14:23.320 --> 14:25.489
The legendary metal.

14:25.573 --> 14:30.703
My Excalibur was forged of orichalcum
by dwarven smiths.

14:30.786 --> 14:33.289
Where did you find this orichalcum?

14:33.372 --> 14:36.458
In the caldera of Mount Volcano.

14:36.542 --> 14:39.587
Where is this Mount Volcano?

14:44.633 --> 14:45.926
A home improvement store.

14:50.764 --> 14:54.393
From what I can tell,
this isn't real orichalcum.

14:54.476 --> 14:56.604
Shut up. What do you know?

14:56.687 --> 14:59.231
It's heat-resistant carbon from
a home improvement store.

14:59.315 --> 15:00.566
I said, shut up!

15:02.109 --> 15:04.528
What are you doing, Vulcan?!

15:04.612 --> 15:05.905
You insult the Knight King!

15:05.988 --> 15:10.326
Hey, Knight King! How about going
to find some real orichalcum with me?

15:10.409 --> 15:13.412
What? What does that mean?

15:13.495 --> 15:16.290
We find the legendary metal.

15:19.710 --> 15:22.504
I'll forge you a real holy sword!

15:29.970 --> 15:31.722
Orichalcum?

15:31.805 --> 15:33.974
Uh… I've never heard of it.

15:34.058 --> 15:37.561
A legendary ore? Does it even exist?

15:37.645 --> 15:38.979
No.

15:41.106 --> 15:42.858
Oh? Yu!

15:43.525 --> 15:48.280
Iris! I received word from Vulcan
and came straight to Asakusa!

15:48.948 --> 15:51.408
I'm so glad that you're doing well!

15:51.492 --> 15:53.744
Thanks to you, I'm doing better than ever!

15:58.123 --> 16:00.209
Then what do we do now, Vulcan?!

16:00.292 --> 16:04.129
You made stuff up to get
Arthur back on his feet?!

16:04.213 --> 16:05.464
Hold on, hear me out.

16:06.173 --> 16:09.593
Arthur gets stronger when his image
of himself as a knight is clearer.

16:09.677 --> 16:11.470
We just need to make him think it's real!

16:11.553 --> 16:12.680
What's that mean?

16:12.763 --> 16:16.308
Basically, we make up a legend ourselves!

16:16.392 --> 16:19.019
We pretend to find real orichalcum.

16:19.103 --> 16:21.063
"We"?

16:21.146 --> 16:23.899
We're included in this game of pretend?

16:23.983 --> 16:25.693
Can you even do this?

16:25.776 --> 16:27.152
We're up against Arthur.

16:27.236 --> 16:29.405
The quality can be low. That's no problem.

16:31.615 --> 16:36.370
After encountering the enemy in Fuchu, we
know that they've got plenty of monsters.

16:36.453 --> 16:41.083
<i>To even the field, we need</i>
<i>to get Arthur to power up!</i>

16:41.667 --> 16:46.130
The 8th needs Arthur to rev up
harder, or we're in trouble.

16:46.714 --> 16:51.677
I understand that it's necessary,
but playing pretend is, well, kind of…

16:51.760 --> 16:55.264
Yes, Yu, it's definitely idiotic.

16:55.848 --> 16:59.935
But it involves Arthur,
so you know normal won't cut it!

17:00.436 --> 17:02.104
Anyway, knock your IQ down a few notches.

17:02.187 --> 17:03.397
Got it?

17:03.480 --> 17:06.358
I have a fake orichalcum ready.

17:06.442 --> 17:08.444
Lisa, Yu, let's go!

17:10.362 --> 17:11.864
Wait a minute!

17:11.947 --> 17:15.242
Knock down my IQ?
How far do I need to drop it?

17:15.325 --> 17:18.495
As low as it takes to
dig up some orichalcum!

17:20.748 --> 17:23.667
He thinks he just said something profound!

17:23.751 --> 17:25.711
Vul's a pretty big idiot too.

17:29.256 --> 17:32.259
EAGER EAGER

17:33.761 --> 17:37.139
All right, Arthur. I brought the party.

17:39.183 --> 17:42.478
We do need a traditional four-man party.

17:43.479 --> 17:45.230
As for what we need to do…

17:45.314 --> 17:47.858
Yes. We need to look for clues.

17:47.941 --> 17:51.278
I heard there's a man
who's familiar with orichalcum.

17:51.361 --> 17:55.365
What? Someone familiar
with the legendary ore?

17:55.449 --> 17:56.992
Who is it?

17:57.868 --> 18:01.914
The owner of the pickle shop knows
a great deal about orichalcum.

18:03.791 --> 18:06.168
Why the owner of a pickle shop?

18:06.251 --> 18:07.961
-Pickles…
-Hey, Vul…

18:08.045 --> 18:10.172
Just look. He's doubting you.

18:10.255 --> 18:11.882
Come on, don't worry!

18:12.549 --> 18:14.051
Just think, Arthur!

18:14.134 --> 18:16.720
You need pickling stones
to pickle, don't you?

18:16.804 --> 18:19.306
Picklers are pros when it comes to stones!

18:19.389 --> 18:22.392
I see! Vulcan, you're a genius!

18:22.476 --> 18:25.771
I hadn't thought of that!
No wonder no one would know!

18:25.854 --> 18:30.901
I had a faint hope for him,
but he's a true blue fool.

18:35.280 --> 18:37.074
TSUKETARO PICKLES

18:37.157 --> 18:40.536
Arthur, this is the place.
Tsuketaro Pickles.

18:43.080 --> 18:46.959
TALK - EXAMINE USE - STRENGTH

18:47.042 --> 18:50.921
Sir, will you tell me
where I can find orichalcum?

18:51.004 --> 18:52.506
Hold on, Arthur!

18:52.589 --> 18:55.092
W-We're so sorry!
That was a really weird question…

18:55.717 --> 18:58.178
The orichalcum is in the kimono shop.

18:58.262 --> 18:59.138
Huh?!

18:59.721 --> 19:02.099
Sir, tell me more!

19:03.142 --> 19:03.976
PEEK

19:04.059 --> 19:04.977
GULP

19:05.853 --> 19:08.564
The orichalcum is in the kimono shop.

19:08.647 --> 19:12.526
He only says the one line!
It's just like in a game!

19:12.609 --> 19:14.862
Vul got them all in on it…

19:14.945 --> 19:17.364
He doesn't think it's at all unnatural?

19:26.415 --> 19:30.085
So even the King of Destruction
likes high places?

19:30.169 --> 19:33.380
I'm figuring out
what I'm gonna break next.

19:34.673 --> 19:37.176
I've always been an outsider.

19:37.759 --> 19:42.472
Nothing changes if I assist
the enemies of the Empire.

19:42.556 --> 19:45.267
Meanwhile, you've taken in the 8th.

19:46.393 --> 19:48.353
Nothing changes in Asakusa either.

19:49.146 --> 19:51.773
This country and this
whole world's all lies.

19:51.857 --> 19:53.567
I'm pissed.

19:54.318 --> 19:57.487
Anyone higher up than me,
stronger than me…

19:58.071 --> 20:02.451
I wanna crush 'em all and protect
everyone weaker than me.

20:03.118 --> 20:09.708
Whatever you do becomes right.
Anyone you crush becomes evil.

20:09.791 --> 20:11.668
That's what makes a king.

20:12.336 --> 20:13.837
The King of Destruction.

20:15.714 --> 20:18.759
The 8th's fixing to start a fight.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.470
There's no way I'm not gonna join it.

20:21.553 --> 20:26.016
So both you and me
are indiscriminate idiots, huh?

20:26.099 --> 20:28.268
Guess there's plenty around if you look.

20:29.269 --> 20:30.187
What?

20:30.270 --> 20:32.022
You say that like there's others.

20:32.689 --> 20:35.692
There are. Idiots like that.

20:35.776 --> 20:39.655
Especially in the Nether
where the light doesn't reach.

20:44.117 --> 20:46.912
That is the legendary shovel.

20:46.995 --> 20:49.456
The barber knows where the orichalcum is.

20:49.539 --> 20:52.668
This is… the legendary shovel!

20:52.751 --> 20:55.045
That is the legendary shovel.

20:55.128 --> 20:56.129
The barber…

20:58.507 --> 21:01.969
You got a whole lot of folks in on this.

21:02.052 --> 21:04.388
The people of Asakusa like a good party.

21:04.471 --> 21:07.349
Hey! What are you dallying for?
Let's get going!

21:07.933 --> 21:10.394
The end of this adventure…

21:10.477 --> 21:13.063
You put the orichalcum
at the end of it, right?

21:13.146 --> 21:15.941
Don't worry.
It's gonna be a good surprise.

21:20.570 --> 21:22.614
This tree is Yggdrasil!

21:22.698 --> 21:26.243
A hint to the whereabouts
of orichalcum lie at its foot…

21:28.120 --> 21:30.289
TALK - EXAMINE USE - STRENGTH

21:32.916 --> 21:34.626
A bag with a paper inside.

21:36.670 --> 21:41.216
<i>I see. So the orichalcum's at</i>
<i>the pickle shop we visited first.</i>

21:41.800 --> 21:44.177
The legends are where you first start out.

21:44.261 --> 21:47.556
It's overplayed, but
Arthur's gonna love it.

21:47.639 --> 21:49.891
It's actually just a lump of iron,

21:49.975 --> 21:53.020
but getting him to solve the riddles'll
make him feel it better

21:53.103 --> 21:54.646
and get his imagination revved up.

21:55.230 --> 21:57.149
"It is dark beneath the lamp post."

21:57.232 --> 22:00.861
I see! So that is where the orichalcum is!

22:00.944 --> 22:03.196
That's right! Let's get going now!

22:03.780 --> 22:08.076
It is dark beneath the lamp post!
So the orichalcum is somewhere dark!

22:08.160 --> 22:09.453
The Nether!

22:10.579 --> 22:12.748
N-No! Check the note again!

22:12.831 --> 22:14.624
It says it's in a shop!

22:14.708 --> 22:18.962
So the legendary ore was in the Nether,
where no one could have seen it before!

22:20.756 --> 22:22.466
He can't hear me…

22:22.549 --> 22:24.509
Vulcan! What do we do now?!

22:24.593 --> 22:25.969
His imagination's way too revved up!

22:26.053 --> 22:28.263
It was too hard for Arthur!

22:28.346 --> 22:31.433
Arthur'd never understand
"It is dark beneath the lamp post"!

22:36.897 --> 22:38.648
Onward and upward! To the Nether!

22:38.732 --> 22:40.400
Hold it!

24:14.494 --> 24:15.662
NEXT TIME

24:17.330 --> 24:19.249
<i>It really is you, Arthur!</i>

24:19.332 --> 24:20.208
<i>Who?!</i>

24:22.127 --> 24:24.880
<i>Next time, "The Holy Sword Reborn."</i>

24:24.963 --> 24:27.716
<i>Return to the great flame of fire.</i> Látom.
